       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. My last message suggested I would, and I shouldn't have said that.\n\n1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the 2,550 mg/day maximum. I know of no indication that supports it. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Discuss it with your attending or pharmacy.** If you think there's a reason to go above the maximum, they can confirm it, and the order can be entered through whatever process your hospital uses for exceptions.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
